moni Mondal and Another reported in</data><data key="d2">1</data></node><node id="prec_1991_3_scc_600"><data key="d0">precedent</data><data key="d1">Sanghi v. High Court of Punjab</data><data key="d2">1</data></node><node id="prec_2006_5_scc_1"><data key="d0">precedent</data><data key="d1">(2006) 5 SCC 1</data><data key="d2">1</data></node><node id="prec_1984_3_scc_405"><data key="d0">precedent</data><data key="d1">prayer to drop the proceedings. The Court took note of the following observations of this Court in L.D. Jaikwal v. State of U.P</data><data key="d2">1</data></node><node id="prec_2013_11_scc_404"><data key="d0">precedent</data><data key="d1">This Court in Priya Gupta and Another v. Additional Secretary</data><data key="d2">1</data></node><node id="prec_air_1989_sc_2185"><data key="d0">precedent</data><data key="d1">Rakapalli Raja Ram Gopala Rao v. Naragani Govinda Sehararao</data><data key="d2">1</data></node><node id="prec_air_1995_sc_308"><data key="d0">precedent</data><data key="d1">Rakapalli Raja Ram Gopala Rao v. Naragani Govinda Sehararao</data><data key="d2">1</data></node><node id="prec_air_2006_sc_258"><data key="d0">precedent</data><data key="d1">mobiles v. S. Moosa</data><data key="d2">1</data></node><node id="prec_air_1950_bom_336"><data key="d0">precedent</data><data key="d1">one rendered by the Bombay High Court and another by the Calcutta High Court. The Bombay High Court in Bajranglal Gangadhar Khemka and another v. Kapurchand Ltd. reported in AIR</data><data key="d2">1</data></node><node id="prec_air_1948_cal_294"><data key="d0">precedent</data><data key="d1">of the Calcutta High Court in Nisha Kanto Roy Chowdhuri v. Smt. Saroj Bashini Goho reported in AIR</data><data key="d2">1</data></node><node id="prec_air_2021_sc_3709"><data key="d0">precedent</data><data key="d1">The decision of this Court is reported in Suman Chadha v. Central Bank of India reported in AIR</data><data key="d2">1</data></node><node id="prec_air_1986_cal_220"><data k